<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: EU farm ministers call for beef support.</title>
<headline>EU farm ministers call for beef support.</headline>
<dateline>KILLARNEY, Ireland 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers called on Tuesday for urgent measures to aid the beef industry because of the BSE crisis and to restore consumer confidence in the meat.</p>
<p>A statement drawn up at an informal three-day meeting of EU agriculture ministers said, &quot;We recognise the extreme urgency of providing sufficient intervention possibilities to avoid dislocation of the beef market.&quot;  </p>
<p>It instructed a committee of experts meeting on October 1 to prepare a text to ensure adequate EU intervention in the market.</p>
<p>It backed the widening of intervention (EU support buying) tenders to include young cattle between seven and nine months old.</p>
<p>Ministers also supported a plan to advance aid payments to beef producers in 1997 to the current year.</p>
<p>EU Agriculture Commissioner Franz Fischler was to explain the measures at a news conference later in the day.</p>
</text>
